### Reference: Translation Examples (Java → Cangjie)
The following are verified translation examples from similar code patterns. Use them as reference.

### Example 1 [general]
// Source: 21-64:Util.33-43:stripLeadingAndTrailingQuotes
```java
static String stripLeadingAndTrailingQuotes(String str) {
        final int length = str.length();
        if (length > 1
                && str.startsWith("\"")
                && str.endsWith("\"")
                && str.substring(1, length - 1).indexOf('"') == -1) {
            str = str.substring(1, length - 1);
        }

        return str;
    }
```
== translates to ==
```cangjie
let length = str.size
if (length > 1 && str.startsWith("\"") && str.endsWith("\"") && str[1..length-1].indexOf('"') == -1) {
return str[1..length-1]
}
return str
```
// [verified] Compile-verified

### Example 2 [general]
// Source: 21-64:Util.51-63:stripLeadingHyphens
```java
static String stripLeadingHyphens(final String str) {
        if (str == null) {
            return null;
        }
        if (str.startsWith("--")) {
            return str.substring(2);
        }
        if (str.startsWith("-")) {
            return str.substring(1);
        }

        return str;
    }
```
== translates to ==
```cangjie
if (str == "") {
return ""
}
if (str.startsWith("--")) {
return str[2..str.size]
}
if (str.startsWith("-")) {
return str[1..str.size]
}
return str
```
// [verified] Compile-verified

